+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Apply a patch without mutating inputs
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` SHALL apply the operations of `patch` (an array) in order, as defined by RFC 6902, and return the resulting document. Neither `document` nor `patch` SHALL be mutated, and the result SHALL NOT share mutable structure with them.
+
+#### Scenario: Input untouched
+- **WHEN** a patch is applied to a document
+- **THEN** the original document is unchanged and the result is a new value
+
+#### Scenario: Atomic failure
+- **WHEN** any operation fails
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and no partial result is returned
+
+### Requirement: Invalid patches are rejected
+`applyPatch` SHALL throw an error when `patch` is not an array, when an operation is not an object, when `op` is missing or not one of the six operations, when `path` is missing or not a valid JSON Pointer string, when `from` (move, copy) is missing or invalid, or when `value` (add, replace, test) is absent.
+
+#### Scenario: Unknown op
+- **WHEN** an operation has `op` `"frob"`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: add
+`add` SHALL set the member of an object (replacing an existing one), insert into an array before the given index (`-` appends; index equal to length appends), or replace the whole document when the path is `""`. It SHALL throw if the parent does not exist, or the array index is malformed or greater than the length.
+
+#### Scenario: Array insert
+- **WHEN** adding `"x"` at `/a/1` to `{"a":["p","q"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":["p","x","q"]}`
+
+### Requirement: remove
+`remove` SHALL delete an existing object member or array element (shifting later elements), and SHALL throw if the target does not exist. Removing the root is allowed and yields `null`.
+
+#### Scenario: Missing target
+- **WHEN** removing `/nope`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: replace
+`replace` SHALL replace the value at an existing location, and SHALL throw if the target does not exist.
+
+#### Scenario: Replace missing
+- **WHEN** replacing `/nope`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: move
+`move` SHALL remove the value at `from` and add it at `path`. It SHALL throw if `from` does not exist, or if `from` is a proper prefix of `path`.
+
+#### Scenario: Move into itself
+- **WHEN** moving `/a` to `/a/b`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: copy
+`copy` SHALL add a deep copy of the value at `from` at `path`, and SHALL throw if `from` does not exist.
+
+#### Scenario: Copy independence
+- **WHEN** an object is copied to a new location and then modified by a later operation
+- **THEN** the original location is unaffected
+
+### Requirement: test
+`test` SHALL succeed only if the value at `path` exists and is deeply equal to `value` per JSON equality (object member order ignored, numbers by value, types distinct); otherwise it SHALL throw.
+
+#### Scenario: Mismatch
+- **WHEN** testing `/a` against a different value
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
